\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Father, let Thy kingdom come,
\par Let it come with living power;
\par Speak at length the final word,
\par Usher in the triumph hour.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. As it came in days of old,
\par In the deepest hearts of men,
\par When Thy martyrs died for Thee,
\par Let it come, O God, again!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Tyrant thrones and idol shrines,
\par Let them from their place be hurled:
\par Enter on Thy better reign,
\par Wear the crown of Thine own  world.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O what long, sad years have gone,
\par Since Thy church was taught this prayer!
\par O what eyes have watched and wept
\par For the dawning everywhere!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Break, triumphant day of God!
\par Break at last, our hearts to cheer;
\par Throbbing souls and holy songs
\par Wait to hail Thy dawning here.
\par       
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 6. Empires, temples, scepters, thrones-
\par May they all for God be won;
\par And, in every human heart,
\par Father, let Thy kingdom come!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

